# Keep the image small, and keep out anything that must never leave this
# machine.
#
# Docker anchors a pattern without ** to the context root, unlike .gitignore,
# which matches at any depth. A plain ".env" here would NOT have excluded
# cira/.env - which is where the real one lives - and the key would have been
# baked into the image and pushed to whatever host it was deployed to.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
venv/
records/
evaluation/
paper/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
